WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.473
The core idea is to raise the network's degrees of
freedom without adding new parameters,

00:00:05.553 --> 00:00:09.278
by letting existing components do more work, as
biology does.

00:00:09.358 --> 00:00:10.838
For local metaplasticity,

00:00:10.918 --> 00:00:16.640
the learning rate alpha is no longer a user-defined
constant but a function of the connection

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:18.200
weight between two nodes,

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:23.690
so the Hebbian update becomes weight-dependent: the
change in a weight equals a function

00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:27.184
of that weight times the product of the two node states.

00:00:27.264 --> 00:00:32.612
This can potentiate co-activated synapses faster
and depress opposing ones more slowly.

00:00:32.692 --> 00:00:34.671
For network-level metaplasticity,

00:00:34.751 --> 00:00:38.414
alpha is instead tied to the change in the
network's energy,

00:00:38.494 --> 00:00:44.091
so learning slows in shallow parts of the energy
landscape and speeds up on steeper slopes,

00:00:44.171 --> 00:00:45.776
helping avoid local minima.

00:00:45.856 --> 00:00:49.769
Homeostasis is approximated by oscillatory
activation functions,

00:00:49.849 --> 00:00:55.072
such as trigonometric ones, and adaptivity is
further supported by modular structure,

00:00:55.152 --> 00:01:01.123
where modules that consistently strengthen their
internal connections receive an automatic boost,

00:01:01.203 --> 00:01:04.430
and inter-module inhibition regulates overall energy.
